    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1944230795537002711",
      "url": "https://x.com/shanaka86/status/1944230795537002711",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/shanaka86/status/1944230795537002711",
      "text": "🚨 SRI LANKA VS. TRUMP TARIFFS: The Hidden War Begins 🇱🇰⚔️🇺🇸\n\nEveryone’s celebrating the “30% win.” But here’s the truth:\n\nSri Lanka dodged a bullet — but may be walking into a minefield.\n\n🧵 The full breakdown of risk, retaliation, and opportunity:\n\n1/\n\n🇱🇰 Trump’s 30% tariff on Sri Lanka (↓ from 44%) was spun as a win.\n\nBut here’s what’s being missed:\n• 🇻🇳 Vietnam got 20% (they agreed to slash US import tariffs)\n• 🇧🇩 Bangladesh faces 35%\n• 🇮🇩 Indonesia: 32%\n• 🇲🇲 Myanmar: 40%\n• 🇵🇭 Philippines: 20%\n\nSri Lanka now sits in a fragile middle-tier of tariff exposure.\n\n2/\n\n📩 Trump’s letter to President Anura Kumara was blunt:\n\n“Our trade has been far from reciprocal. Starting August 1, 2025, we will charge 30% on all Sri Lankan products — separate from sectoral tariffs. Any retaliation = escalation.”\n\nTranslation: This is not diplomacy. It’s a hostage negotiation.\n\n3/\n\n🧨 Even worse: the U.S. offered Sri Lanka a backdoor deal — reduce trade with China in exchange for lower tariffs.\n\nBut Sri Lanka said no — citing its non-aligned foreign policy.\n\nThat principle may cost billions.\n\n4/\n\n🔥 India is circling.\n\n🇮🇳 According to Delhi trade data, India could cannibalize $618M of Sri Lanka’s U.S. exports — from shirts to sapphires, nightwear to tea.\n\nAnd they haven’t even struck a US trade deal yet.\n\nIf India does, Sri Lanka could lose 21% of its U.S. market share.\n\n5/\n\n🇨🇦 Reminder: Canada imposed a digital tax on U.S. tech firms.\n\nTrump ended trade talks, threatened tariffs within 7 days, and forced Canada to scrap its tax.\n\nSri Lanka? We’re imposing an 18% digital VAT on U.S. giants right now — for a measly $32M (0.04% of GDP).\n\nThe risk?\n📉 Lose $3B in U.S. exports\n📈 Trigger a 48% total tariff bomb\n\n6/\n\n🧬 All this while IMF reforms extract every ounce of liquidity:\n\n• CBSL bond sale undersubscribed (LKR 142B raised vs LKR 200B offered)\n• IMF EFF pushing SOE restructuring, FX borrowing limits, and VAT expansions\n• SriLankan Airlines faces court freeze — and bondholder wind-up threats\n\nBalance sheet fragility + export shock = dual system stress\n\n7/\n\n📦 Sri Lankan exporters are now sounding alarms:\n\n“The 30% tariff is unsustainable. Vietnam and India are getting better deals. We must diversify markets — urgently.”\n\nBut that’s a tough pivot in a deflationary, de-globalizing trade world.\n\n8/\n\n📊 This isn’t just a tariff hike. It’s a systemic exposure test.\n\nIf Sri Lanka:\n• Fails to renegotiate\n• Triggers digital tax retaliation\n• Lets India seize apparel and gem orders\n\n…we may lose strategic export dominance in under 90 days.\n\n9/\n\n🇬🇧 Meanwhile, UK opens its doors — duty-free access for 🇱🇰 garments under new liberal rules of origin. DCTS framework starts 2026.\n\nA glimmer of hope — but a long runway.\n\n10/\n\n🔮 What must be done?\n\n• Immediately postpone the 18% digital VAT\n• Reopen US tariff talks — offer para-tariff elimination in exchange\n• Protect apparel sector liquidity + FX buffers\n• Shield digital exporters from VAT passthroughs\n• Segment domestic vs external balance sheets in fiscal strategy\n\n11/\n\n💣 Final truth:\n\nSri Lanka’s 30% tariff win is not a victory.\n\nIt’s a countdown.\n\n⏳ We’re in a tariff sniper zone between China, India, Vietnam, and Trump’s doctrine of reciprocity.\n\nSmart geopolitics, not spreadsheet compliance, will determine who survives.\n\n#SriLanka #TrumpTariffs #DigitalVAT #IMF #Macro #Exports #China #India #US #CSE #Policy #GeoTrade #TradeWar #colombo #LKA #Srilankanews",
